Paddle.update: we need to handle horizontal movement with acceleration.

We have vx and ax. In our simplified version we used vx directly; but we need to incorporate acceleration.

Let's rewrite Paddle.update:

```
update(dt) {
  // horizontal movement based on mouse
  const targetX = this.game.input.mouseX - this.game.canvas.width/2;
  const dx = targetX - this.x;
  // accelerate towards target
  if (dx > 0) {
    this.ax = this.CONFIG.paddleAcc * dt;
  } else if (dx < 0) {
    this.ax = -this.CONFIG.paddleAcc * dt;
  } else {
    this.ax = 0;
  }
  // apply acceleration to velocity
  this.vx += this.ax;
  // clamp speed
  if (this.vx > this.CONFIG.maxPaddleSpeed) this.vx = this.CONFIG.maxPaddleSpeed;
  if (this.vx < -this.CONFIG.maxPaddleSpeed) this.vx = -this.CONFIG.maxPaddleSpeed;
  // integrate position
  this.x += this.vx * dt;
  // clamp to canvas
  const halfW = this.width/2;
  if (this.x - halfW < 0) this.x = halfW;
  if (this.x + halfW > this.game.canvas.width) this.x = this.game.canvas.width - halfW;
  // rotation
  this.rotationSpeed = this.game.input.rotateSpeed;
  this.angle += this.rotationSpeed * dt;
  // clamp angle
  this.angle = Math.max(-Math.PI/4, Math.min(Math.PI/4, this.angle));
}
```

